WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.440
Eighty thousand monkeys.

2
00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.030
One way out.

3
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.890
A Buddhist Jataka tells of a

4
00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.130
monkey king, whose troop lived

5
00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.330
in a great mango tree beside the

6
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:12.280
Ganga.

7
00:00:12.641 --> 00:00:15.121
One ripe mango fell into the

8
00:00:15.121 --> 00:00:17.481
river, and floated down to the

9
00:00:17.481 --> 00:00:19.031
king of Benares.

10
00:00:19.603 --> 00:00:22.323
He tasted it, and sailed upriver

11
00:00:22.323 --> 00:00:23.913
to find the tree.

12
00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:26.634
At midnight he woke to monkeys

13
00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:28.194
feeding above him.

14
00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.474
"Surround the tree," he told his

15
00:00:30.474 --> 00:00:31.564
archers.

16
00:00:32.037 --> 00:00:34.457
"Do not fear," said the monkey

17
00:00:34.457 --> 00:00:36.817
king. And he leapt across the

18
00:00:36.817 --> 00:00:37.667
river.

19
00:00:38.094 --> 00:00:40.254
He tied a long bamboo to a

20
00:00:40.254 --> 00:00:42.274
tree there, and to his own

21
00:00:42.274 --> 00:00:44.344
waist, and leapt back.

22
00:00:44.865 --> 00:00:46.685
The bamboo fell short.

23
00:00:46.685 --> 00:00:48.705
So he caught a branch with both

24
00:00:48.705 --> 00:00:50.465
hands, and held.

25
00:00:50.465 --> 00:00:52.955
His own body became the bridge.

26
00:00:53.627 --> 00:00:56.447
Across his back, the whole troop

27
00:00:56.447 --> 00:00:57.967
reached safety.

28
00:00:57.967 --> 00:01:00.267
One leapt down hard upon him,

29
00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.137
and his heart broke.

30
00:01:02.715 --> 00:01:05.235
At daybreak the king, who had

31
00:01:05.235 --> 00:01:07.715
watched it all, had him brought

32
00:01:07.715 --> 00:01:09.065
down gently.

33
00:01:09.682 --> 00:01:11.722
"You made yourself a bridge for

34
00:01:11.722 --> 00:01:12.942
them," he said.

35
00:01:12.942 --> 00:01:15.082
"What are you to them, and what

36
00:01:15.082 --> 00:01:16.452
are they to you?"

37
00:01:17.029 --> 00:01:18.649
"I am their chief.

38
00:01:18.649 --> 00:01:21.469
Their happiness is won, so I do

39
00:01:21.469 --> 00:01:22.819
not fear death."

40
00:01:23.343 --> 00:01:24.683
He died there.

41
00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:26.823
The king honoured him as a king,

42
00:01:26.823 --> 00:01:29.673
and ruled justly all his life.

43
00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.910
The scene was carved in stone at

44
00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.230
Bharhut, over two thousand years

45
00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:37.063
ago. For GS4:

46
00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.750
power is a duty to those you

47
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:40.550
lead.

48
00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:42.759
One night.

49
00:01:42.759 --> 00:01:44.139
One bridge.

50
00:01:44.139 --> 00:01:46.379
And a king who learned what a

51
00:01:46.379 --> 00:01:47.849
ruler owes.
